  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% benchmark but removes any sales stop, and customers receive full per-model numeric results while the public does not, which satisfies both NW-1 and HC-1. S5 makes recall mandatory at 8 per 100k on verified model-level rates with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) while leaving Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.4) clear. S1 is limited to serious incidents with no deadline for other thermal incidents, which benefits both firms given their unreported incidents."
